From d257cb0ed8092e787c44648375791d4a5c348321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vera-Parity <vera-parity@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:43:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add label-cap boundary cases (15 / 16 labels) to the
 diff4 suite.

Surface: exactly 15 labels (6 value if_pos + 1 while) passes on all four
backends; 16 is rejected by the surface frontend (alloc_lbl next_lbl > 15,
ids start at 1 -> error[BUDGET_EXCEEDED]).
Assembly (new '#asm' source form in the harness): exactly 16 labels with
ids 0..15, and 15 labels with ids 0..14, are accepted by the Rust binary
verifier, lockstep, the Phase-7 kernel and the Omni engine, and run
correctly on VM / Wasm / x86-64 / Stage-1 (Stage-1 ELF == host ELF).
So the 15-label limit is a frontend limit, not an emit limit. The 16 vs 15
cap is an open decision; the 16-label expectations are marked as such.

The harness Stage-1 leg now takes the u16 stream directly
(compile_u16_via_stage1_to_elf_for_diff, same gates as
compile_omni_surface_via_stage1_to_elf). Frontend rejections can be
graded with DiffExpect::Rejected. Suite: 109 graded (74 pass, 35 xfail). Selftest 556 -> 572.
Frozen hashes unchanged.
